From 853830028278296e08ae9edc35106020073f191c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 15:30:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix unstyled pages on Railway: trust the proxy's https scheme

Railway ends TLS at its proxy, so Laravel saw http and asset() built http:// stylesheet links that the browser blocked as mixed content on the https page. Trust X-Forwarded-For/-Port/-Proto from the proxy (never -Host, which would let a header choose the school) and force https in production. Adds tests, docs, smoke-test steps and an .env.example note.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
