+Every tenant-owned Eloquent model uses `App\Models\Concerns\BelongsToTenant`. Never query across tenants by bypassing that global scope except in explicit, reviewed super-admin/system operations. Resolve tenants by subdomain/custom domain (`ResolveTenant`); there is no header or session override, and none may be added. Behind Railway's proxy only `X-Forwarded-For/-Port/-Proto` are trusted (`bootstrap/app.php`); never trust `X-Forwarded-Host`, since the host picks the school. Use `TenantContext::run()` for scoped work and do not retain context between requests or jobs. With no tenant, scoped queries return nothing; `TenantContext::runAsSystem()` is the only way to see all schools and needs a reason in review. Queued work uses the `TenantAwareJob` trait (`RestoreTenantContext` middleware); serialized queue payloads carry the tenant ID only. Tenant ids are ULIDs. Permissions use Spatie Permission in teams mode keyed by tenant: `TenantTeamResolver` takes the team only from `TenantContext`, every school has the five roles in `config/roles.php` (`SyncTenantRoles`, additive only), and a permission is added to that file only with the feature that checks it. Assign roles by name or id inside the school's context. `User` is the one tenant-owned model without `BelongsToTenant` (it uses `UserScope`: a school sees its own users, the central domain only super-admins); `tenant_id` and `is_super_admin` are never mass assignable.
 
